              "schema:description": "ArF 193 nm excimer laser with a HelEx sample cell, coupled to the mass spectrometer through an aerosol rapid introduction system (ARIS) giving sub-second washout. Constant energy set 7 mJ, laser energy 100% (open gate), repetition rate 7 Hz, beam diameter 30 um. Helium carrier via two mass flow controllers, MFC1 0.10 and MFC2 0.30 l/min."
            },
            {
              "@type": [
                "schema:Thing",
                "schema:Product"
              ],
              "schema:additionalType": [
                {
                  "@id": "nxs:base_classes/NXinstrument.html"
                },
                "ICPMS",
                "Laser Ablation System",
                {
                  "@id": "https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q3099911"
                }
              ],
              "schema:name": "Nu Instruments HR Multi-collector",
              "schema:identifier": [
                "ex:instrument-ada-001"
              ],
              "@id": "ex:instrument/nxs-BaseClass-NXinstrument",
              "schema:manufacturer": {
                "@type": [
                  "schema:Organization"
                ],
                "schema:name": "Nu Instruments"
              },
              "schema:model": {
                "@type": [
                  "schema:ProductModel"
                ],
                "schema:name": "Nu Plasma HR"
              },
              "schema:description": "High-resolution multi-collector ICP-MS. RF power 1300 W; cool gas 13.0, auxiliary 0.80, sample/make-up 1.06 l/min. Combined Faraday and ion-counter routine. Collector configuration, mass by cup: ExH = 238U (Faraday); H2 = 232Th (Faraday); L6 = 208Pb (Faraday); L7 = 207Pb (Faraday); L8 = 206Pb (Faraday); IC0 = 204Pb (ion counter); IC2 = 202Hg + Pb (ion counter)."
            }
          ]
        }
